        {
            "number": 6,
            "revision": "11eb6574a6858604a8b2648eaf67b3eb5d314ed4",
            "parents": [
                "3d5062804ce3eb4f198ffd2bed2f4f4876af8aee"
            ],
            "ref": "refs/changes/27/78827/6",
            "uploader": {
                "name": "Patrick NC Lin",
                "email": "patrick.nc.lin.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                "username": "PatrickLinww"
            },
            "createdOn": 1741748609,
            "author": {
                "name": "Patrick NC Lin",
                "email": "patrick.nc.lin.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                "username": "PatrickLinww"
            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "bmc_state_manager.cpp",
                    "line": 279,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Geissler",
                        "email": "geissonator@yahoo.com",
                        "username": "geissonator"
                    },
                    "message": "If someone just does a bmc \"reboot\" or a BMC goes through a code update and reboots as a part of the update, our systems would not want an error at the Notice level. I think we need to distinguish between a \"normal\" reboot and an error reboot when it comes to the Level."
                },
                {
                    "file": "bmc_state_manager.cpp",
                    "line": 279,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick NC Lin",
                        "email": "patrick.nc.lin.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                        "username": "PatrickLinww"
                    },
                    "message": "Hi @geissonator@yahoo.com,\nWe believe that an event log should be generated for all types of BMC reboots, regardless of whether it is a normal reboot or an error-related reboot. As for how to distinguish between normal and error reboots, we are currently discussing the best approach with other maintainers. Once we reach a conclusion, we will provide an update.\n\nIn the meantime, you can refer to the ongoing discussion at the following link: https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/docs/+/76410\nhttps://lore.kernel.org/all/9565c496-44d8-4214-8038-931926210d0f@roeck-us.net/"
                },
                {
                    "file": "bmc_state_manager.cpp",
                    "line": 279,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                }
            ],
